on located 3 0cm lateral from the nipple  Sectioning beneath the previous incision reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm hemorrhagic  fragmented previous biopsy site which comes within 1 0cm of the closest deep resection margin  The biopsy cavity is located 6 0cm from the lateral margin  8 5cm from the medial margin  8 0cm from the superior margin and 6 5cm from the inferior margin  The parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is composed predominantly of firm fibrous tissue with a few scattered blue domed cysts  The remaining parenchyma is composed predominantly of lobulated fat interspersed with dense white fibrous septae  No additional masses are noted  There is an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail from which multiple lymph nodes are identified measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Section code  D E  Biopsy cavity in relation to closest deep margin F H  Additional sections of biopsy cavity I J  Fibrous sections of medial parenchyma K  Representative section of lateral parenchyma L O  Representative sections of lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm lymph node with a small amount of attached fat which is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which four lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 2cm in greatest dimension up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm Representative sections of each lymph node are submitted in cassette Q  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D             